{
  "title": "__SYSTEM_NAME__",
  "uid": "system-__SYSTEM_ID__",
  "tags": ["onboarding", "__SYSTEM_TYPE__"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": { "from": "now-6h", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "Environment",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "__ENV_OPTIONS__",
        "current": {},
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "System",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 8, "h": 7 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**__SYSTEM_NAME__** (`__SYSTEM_ID__`, type `__SYSTEM_TYPE__`)\n\nTenant: `__TENANT_ID__`\n\nOwner: __OWNER_TEAM__ (__OWNER_CONTACT__)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Configured Ingestion Budget",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": { "x": 8, "y": 0, "w": 9, "h": 7 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "__BUDGET_TABLE__\n\nRendered from the manifest at generation time - not a live query. See **Ingestion Budget Usage** alongside for the live percentage."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Ingestion Budget Usage (per Signal)",
      "description": "This tenant's real ingested volume since local midnight (Europe/Zurich), as a percentage of EACH signal's own daily budget - Metrics (Mimir), Logs (Loki), Traces (Tempo), Profiles (Pyroscope) each shown as its own line. Both values read directly from two gauges scripts/ingestion-midnight-snapshot.py pushes every 2 minutes (demo_ingestion_since_midnight, demo_ingestion_daily_budget) - no subtraction on this panel's own side (NFR-05 SECOND pre-test audit round, fixed here: this used to recompute \"current minus a separately-pushed day-start snapshot\" in this panel's OWN PromQL, independently of - and able to silently disagree with - the enforcer's own decision, with its own version of that script's pre-fix reset-insensitivity; both now read the exact same, already-correct value). Green below 80%, yellow 80-90%, red above 90%. Same formula as the Operator: Tenant Ingestion Budget dashboard's own panel, filtered to this one tenant. Queried via the Mimir-anonymous datasource, not __DATASOURCE_MIMIR__ - see README.md's Multi-Tenancy section for why (self-monitoring metrics land under the anonymous tenant).",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-anonymous",
      "gridPos": { "x": 17, "y": 0, "w": 7, "h": 7 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 120,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 80 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 90 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom" },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "single" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "expr": "100 * demo_ingestion_since_midnight{tenant=~\"__TENANT_ID__\"} / on(tenant, signal) demo_ingestion_daily_budget{tenant=~\"__TENANT_ID__\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{signal}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 60,
      "title": "Connection Usage",
      "description": "Active backends as a percentage of postgresql_connection_max (server-wide, not per-database - joined with on() group_left() since it carries no database label; max() keeps exactly one series even when a collector restart briefly yields two).",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 7, "w": 8, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "percent", "min": 0, "max": 100 }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "100 * sum by (postgresql_database_name) (postgresql_backends) / on() group_left() max(postgresql_connection_max)",
          "legendFormat": "{{postgresql_database_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 61,
      "title": "Transaction Rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 8, "y": 7, "w": 8, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "ops" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (postgresql_database_name) (rate(postgresql_commits_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{postgresql_database_name}} commits"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (postgresql_database_name) (rate(postgresql_rollbacks_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{postgresql_database_name}} rollbacks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 62,
      "title": "Cache Hit Ratio",
      "description": "Share of block reads served from cache (heap_hit+idx_hit) vs. disk - low/dropping values are worth investigating (undersized shared_buffers, cold cache after restart, etc.).",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 16, "y": 7, "w": 8, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "percent", "min": 0, "max": 100 }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (postgresql_database_name) (rate(postgresql_blocks_read_total{source=~\"heap_hit|idx_hit\"}[5m])) / sum by (postgresql_database_name) (rate(postgresql_blocks_read_total[5m])) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "{{postgresql_database_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 63,
      "title": "Database Size",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 15, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "bytes" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "postgresql_db_size_bytes",
          "legendFormat": "{{postgresql_database_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 64,
      "title": "Table Sizes",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 12, "y": 15, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "bytes" },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "postgresql_table_name" },
            "properties": [{ "id": "displayName", "value": "Table" }, { "id": "unit", "value": "none" }]
          },
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "postgresql_database_name" },
            "properties": [{ "id": "displayName", "value": "Database" }, { "id": "unit", "value": "none" }]
          },
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "Value" },
            "properties": [{ "id": "displayName", "value": "Size" }]
          }
        ]
      },
      "transformations": [
        { "id": "organize", "options": { "excludeByName": { "Time": true }, "indexByName": {}, "renameByName": {} } }
      ],
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "postgresql_table_size_bytes", "format": "table", "instant": true }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 65,
      "title": "Live/Dead Rows by Table",
      "description": "A growing dead-row count relative to live rows suggests autovacuum isn't keeping up.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 23, "w": 24, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "postgresql_rows",
          "legendFormat": "{{postgresql_table_name}} ({{state}})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Recent Traces",
      "description": "A table, not the \"traces\" panel type - Grafana's traces panel silently renders zero rows when Tempo's search response omits durationMs (happens for very fast, sub-millisecond traces), even though the underlying data is there. A table shows the same rows regardless.",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_TEMPO__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 31, "w": 24, "h": 8 },
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "queryType": "traceql", "query": "{} with (most_recent=true)", "limit": 20, "tableType": "traces" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Log Volume by Namespace",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_LOKI__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 39, "w": 24, "h": 8 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (k8s_namespace_name) (count_over_time({k8s_namespace_name=~\".+\"}[$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{k8s_namespace_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Recent Logs",
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_LOKI__",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 47, "w": 24, "h": 8 },
      "options": { "showTime": true, "wrapLogMessage": true, "sortOrder": "Descending" },
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "{k8s_namespace_name=~\".+\"}" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
